          %p
          %h2#section_Ideas Ideas
          %p
            In any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            out there, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate+logic"} predicate logic
            used to define the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            induced by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingletons"} subsingletons
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+sets"} support sets
            of the set theory. This article will describe the internal logic of set theory, in the language of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory#logic+over+type+theory"} predicate logic over set theory
          %p
          %h2#section_Families_of_sets Families of sets
          %p
            We begin with the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/families+of+sets"} families of sets
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+sets"} indexed sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            at an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            is the set of all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            such that
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a) = b
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a \in A \vert f(a) = b\}
          %p
            This could be thought of in turn as a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_b
            indexed by the element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_b \coloneqq \{a \in A \vert f(a) = b\}
          %p
            The whole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
            of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_b)_{b \in B}
            is then the family of sets.
          %p
          %h2#section_Indexed_disjoint_unions_and_cartesian_products Indexed disjoint unions and cartesian products
          %p
            Given a family of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_i)_{i \in I}
            indexed by the set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, a)
            consisting of an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            and an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S_i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \biguplus_{i \in I} S_i \coloneqq \{(i, a) \vert i \in I, a \in S_i\}
          %p
            The indexed cartesian product is defined as the set of all pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, f)
            consisting of an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:I \to S_i
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in I} S_i \coloneqq \{(i, f) \vert i \in I, f:I \to S_i\}
          %p
          %h2#section_Subsingletons_and_singletons Subsingletons and singletons
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            which has at most one element: every two elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in S
            are equal to each other
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isSubsingleton
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isSubsingleton}(S) \coloneqq \forall a \in S.\forall b \in S. a = b
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed
            subsingleton. Equivalently, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+set"} pointed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with specified element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            such that every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in S
            is equal to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            where there exists an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            such that every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in S
            is equal to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isSingleton
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isSingleton}(S) \coloneqq \exists a \in S.\forall b \in S. a = b
          %p
            Every subsingleton is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
          %p
            In the internal logic of set theory, subsingletons represent the internal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            represents the internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singletons"} singletons
            represent the internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
          %p
            Since any family of sets is defined by the fibers of a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            are all subsingletons. However, that is just the requirement that the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \simeq B
          %p
          %h2#section_Support_of_a_set Support of a set
          %p
            Every set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has a unique function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:S \to 1
            into any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            with point
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \in 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u(a) = *
            for all elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
          %p
            Recall that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            is the subset of all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            which are of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a)
            for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} image
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{image}(f) \coloneqq \{f(a) \vert a \in A, f:A \to B\}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the set is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of the unique function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:S \to 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S] \coloneqq \{u(a) \vert a \in S, u:S \to 1\}
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            is always a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of a set is thus a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
          %p
            One could also apply the support to any family of sets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_b)_{b \in S}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([S_b])_{b \in S}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image+factorization"} image factorization
            of every function into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
          %p
          %h2#section_Internal_logical_operators Internal logical operators
          %p
            Supports are important because they will allow us to define the logical operators
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implication"} implication
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+equivalence"} logical equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantification"} universal quantification
            internal to the set theory:
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
            of two subsingletons is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of the two subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \wedge B \coloneqq [A \times B]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            of two subsingletons is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of the two subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊎
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \vee B \coloneqq [A \uplus B]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implication"} implication
            of two subsingletons is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            of the two subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \implies B \coloneqq [B^A]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            of two subsingletons is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
            of the two subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \iff B \coloneqq [A \simeq B]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            of a subsingleton is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            into the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi ∅
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A \coloneqq [\emptyset^A]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            of a family of subsingletons
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_b)_{b \in B}
            ranging over the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of the family of subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo .
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi b
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists b \in B.S_b \coloneqq \left[\biguplus_{b \in B} S_b\right]
          %p
            The logical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantification"} universal quantification
            of a family of subsingletons
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_b)_{b \in B}
            ranging over the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
            of the indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of the family of subsingletons:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo .
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi b
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi b
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall b \in B.S_b \coloneqq \left[\prod_{b \in B} S_b\right]
          %p
            All these operations are not restricted only to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingletons"} subsingletons
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
          %p
          %h2#section_Internal_equality Internal equality
          %p
            The internal equality relation in a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is represented by the initial reflexive graph structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %em graph structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            we mean a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and a pair of function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:R \to S
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t:R \to S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is called the
            %em carrier set
            of the graph structure. We do not assume the two functions are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jointly+monic"} jointly injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+pseudograph"} directed pseudograph
            structures. By a
            = succeed "," do
              %em reflexive graph structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{refl}:S \to R
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(\mathrm{refl}(a)) = a
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(\mathrm{refl}(a)) = a
          %p
            A
            %em graph structure homomorphism
            between two graph structures on the carrier set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, s, t)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,', s', t')
            is a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: R \to R'
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'(f(p)) = s(p)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t'(f(p)) = t(p)
          %p
            A
            %em reflexive graph structure homomorphism
            is a graph structure homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:R \to R'
            between two graph structures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, s, t, \mathrm{refl})
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R', s', t', \mathrm{refl}')
            on a carrier set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            where additionally, for every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
            of the carrier set,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\mathrm{refl}(a)) = \mathrm{refl}'(f(a))
          %p
            A reflexive graph structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{Id}_S, s_{\mathrm{Id}}, t_{ \mathrm{Id}}, \mathrm{refl}_S)
            on a carrier set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is an
            %em initial reflexive graph structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            if for every other reflexive graph structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, s, t, \mathrm{refl})
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathrm{Id}_S \to R
          %p
            Every set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has an initial reflexive graph structure given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+function"} diagonal function
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            It could be shown from this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            that the functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_\mathrm{Id}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_\mathrm{Id}
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jointly+monic"} jointly injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"} axiom K
            holds internally in set theory.
          %p
          %h2#section_Internal_and_external_axioms Internal and external axioms
          %p
            Since every logical operation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate+logic"} predicate logic
            have been internalized in the set theory itself, one then has to distinguish between the axioms written in the external predicate logic used to define the set theory, and the axioms written in the predicate logic internal to the set theory.
          %p
            For example, the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+double+negation"} law of double negation
            states that for any proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            the double negation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            implies
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \neg P \implies P
            %strong internal law of double negation
            would say that for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \neg S \implies S
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            there is an element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} doubleneg
                      %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{doubleneg}_S \in \neg \neg [S] \implies [S]
          %p
            Similarly, the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
            states that for any proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            it is possible to derive that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \vee \neg P
            %strong internal law of excluded middle
            would say that for every for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \vee \neg S
            is a singleton, or equivalently, that for every set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} lem
                      %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{lem}_S \in[S] \vee \neg [S]
